<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 9.921 percent on Monday from 9.925 percent at the previous auction on March 10.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 878.175 million pounds, replace bills worth 849.975 million maturing on Tuesday. The treasury had asked for 800 million pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Sept 16, 1997 (Sept 9, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.921 percent (9.925)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 878.175 million (751.450 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,074.250 million (1,676.650 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.501-9.999 percent (9.701-9.946)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.501-10.200 percent (9.701-10.101)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 154 (55)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 164 (177)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
</text>
